      "description": "Repository health reports for THIS repository: the one `health-report/v1` document `bun run cat-harness-tools/test/health/run.ts --instance <this instance>` writes. Each repository the separation made is its own clone, with its own size, publish branch, branches and stores, so each carries its own report (owner, 2026-10-10: \"All repos need health check\"). The graph typology is cat-harness's; its `health` entry says what separates a health report (about the repository) from a `qa` verdict (about an artefact). It sits at the root, not under `test/health/results/` as in cat-harness, because this instance declares `test/` as code and a declared directory nested inside another is the layout-norms defect (owner, 2026-10-10: option A, move it out of `test/`); at the root a state graph's path equals its id, as `beans/` does.",
